      "about": "which text counts as a number formatted as text",
      "decided": "A text cell whose trimmed text is a plain number, with an optional sign and a decimal point or comma (12.50, 12,50, 2), gets the formatted-as-text refusal; other text, such as \"12,50 EUR\" or \"twelve\", keeps the not-a-number refusal. Calc saves a text-formatted number and an apostrophe-typed one alike, and the fix given (set the category Number, type the value again) mends both, so reading the cell's style adds nothing the colleague gets.",
      "at": "invoicer/sheet.py:23"
